{"name":"Light Curd","hex":"#f9e9c9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"curd","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The coagulated part of any liquid.\nThe part of milk that coagulates when it sours or is treated with enzymes; used to make cottage cheese, dahi, etc.\n\n Dahi.\nA solid piece of coagulated scrambled egg.","The part of milk that coagulates when it sours or is treated with enzymes; used to make cottage cheese, dahi, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form curd; to curdle.","To cause to coagulate or thicken; to cause to congeal; to curdle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/curd"}],"entries":[{"title":"Curd","blocks":[{"text":"Curd is obtained by coagulating milk in a sequential process called curdling. It can be a final dairy product or the first stage in cheesemaking. The coagulation can be caused by adding rennet, a culture, or any edible acidic substance such as lemon juice or vinegar, and then allowing it to coagulate. The increased acidity causes the milk proteins (casein) to tangle into solid masses, or curds. Milk that has been left to sour will also automatically produce curds, and sour milk cheeses are produced this way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Curd_Setting.jpg/330px-Curd_Setting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curd","wikidata":"Q622563"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg/500px-Fabrication_du_Beaufort_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Heating and stirring the curd in the traditional process to make French Beaufort cheese, an Alpine cheese","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFabrication_du_Beaufort_(11).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg/500px-20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg/1280px-20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg/500px-20130911-OC-RBN-3855_%289733481041%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cutting of milk curd into small cubes us